object_location:
Extract object-location observations supported by the normalized episode. Return exactly a JSON object with entities (a list) and edges (an empty list). Each entity must contain name, summary, object, relation, location, observation_kind, evidence_event_ids, and observed_at. Example output shape: {"entities":[{"name":"observation-1","summary":"Watch was observed on desk.","object":"watch 1","relation":"on","location":"desk 1","observation_kind":"found","evidence_event_ids":["EXACT_RESULT_EVENT_ID"],"observed_at":null}],"edges":[]}. Use actual episode values, never the example IDs. Do not output a schema, entity_type, type, source, properties, dynamic_property or episode_record. The compiler generates storage metadata. Optional position requires coordinates already present in cited evidence plus real frame, unit and source. Never guess coordinates or permanent location. Return empty entities when absent.
Timestamp: {dialogue_timestamp}
Provenance: {provenance}
Episode: {chat_chunk}

search_observation:
Extract search observations supported by a real tool result in the normalized episode. Return exactly a JSON object with entities (a list) and edges (an empty list). Each entity contains name, summary, object, location, result, search_action, evidence_event_ids, observed_at. Example output shape: {"entities":[{"name":"search-1","summary":"Watch was found on desk.","object":"watch 1","location":"desk 1","result":"found","search_action":{"tool_call_id":"EXACT_TOOL_CALL_ID"},"evidence_event_ids":["EXACT_RESULT_EVENT_ID"],"observed_at":null}],"edges":[]}. Use actual episode values, never the example IDs. search_action contains ONLY tool_call_id copied from episode.tool_steps; the compiler retrieves real tool and arguments. Evidence must cite this exact call or result. Do not write action labels such as navigate, take or put as search_action. result must be found, not_found, blocked or error. Do not infer absence from an unrelated action or classify manipulation failures as searches. Do not output a schema, entity_type, type, source, properties, dynamic_property or episode_record. Return empty entities when no search observation is evidenced.
Timestamp: {dialogue_timestamp}
Provenance: {provenance}
Episode: {chat_chunk}

task_procedure:
Extract one task-trajectory candidate supported by the normalized episode. Return exactly a JSON object with entities (a list) and edges (an empty list). Each entity contains name, summary, task, target, outcome, steps, evidence_event_ids, outcome_evidence_event_ids, failure_lesson. Example output shape: {"entities":[{"name":"task-1","summary":"Observed attempt; outcome unverified.","task":"put watch on safe","target":"safe 1","outcome":"unknown","steps":[{"tool_call_id":"EXACT_TOOL_CALL_ID"}],"evidence_event_ids":["EXACT_EVENT_ID"],"outcome_evidence_event_ids":[],"failure_lesson":null,"reusable_tool_call_ids":[]}],"edges":[]}. Use actual episode values, never example IDs. Each steps item contains ONLY tool_call_id copied from episode.tool_steps. Include all observed tool calls in original order, including failures and corrections. Do not generate index, tool, arguments, result or status; the compiler copies those from the exact referenced trace. outcome is success, failure, partial or unknown; individual tool success does not establish task success. Empty outcome_evidence_event_ids when no external outcome evidence exists. failure_lesson is null for unknown or unsupported causes; otherwise an object with summary and evidence_event_ids grounded in explicit evidence, never a string. Do not output schema, entity_type, type, source, properties, dynamic_property, episode_record, reusable_steps or is_executable. Only when authoritative task success is evidenced, propose reusable_tool_call_ids referencing successful steps in their original order; otherwise use an empty list. The compiler verifies goal evidence and every referenced step before allowing execution. Return empty entities when absent.
Timestamp: {dialogue_timestamp}
Provenance: {provenance}
Episode: {chat_chunk}
